Composery product identity: what the assembled IDE calls itself and shows.

- product.json coordinates: documentation and newsletter URLs, the trusted
  domain, the server data folder.
- The brand icon wherever upstream draws its own: the letterpress backgrounds
  (editor and sessions, light/dark/high-contrast) and the window icon.
- The titlebar home button and its context menu.
- Composery Dark / Composery Light as the default colour themes, including
  upstream's synchronous first-paint snapshot retinted from the
  composery-themes values. The "default color theme" test fails if that
  snapshot drifts from the theme JSONs, because nothing else would notice a
  first paint in the wrong colours.

Renames are deliberately absent: rebrand.mjs owns every code-server -> Composery
substitution on the assembled tree, so this patch carries only what a rename
rule cannot express.

